unemployed|without-a-job|ADJECTIVE|without paid work|Without a paid job, although able and available to work.|thất nghiệp|After the factory closed, he was unemployed for several months.|Sau khi nhà máy đóng cửa, anh thất nghiệp trong vài tháng.|Usually predicative; unemployed workers. The unemployed refers collectively to people without work.|0
west|western-direction|NOUN|western direction|The direction where the sun appears to set.|phía tây|The lake lies to the west of the railway station.|Hồ nằm về phía tây của nhà ga.|Usually the west; to the west of a place. Lowercase for a compass direction, unless part of a proper name.|0
west|western-side|ADJECTIVE|on the western side|On or towards the western side of a place.|ở phía tây|The west entrance remains open during the renovation.|Lối vào phía tây vẫn mở trong thời gian sửa chữa.|Before a noun: west entrance, west coast. Western is also an adjective, with context-dependent usage.|1
west|towards-west|ADVERB|towards the west|In or towards the western direction.|về phía tây|The walkers headed west after crossing the bridge.|Những người đi bộ hướng về phía tây sau khi qua cầu.|Head west, travel west; no to is needed before this directional adverb.|2
conservation|protecting-nature|NOUN|protection of nature|The protection and careful management of wildlife and natural environments.|sự bảo tồn thiên nhiên|The village supports forest conservation through a community nursery.|Ngôi làng hỗ trợ việc bảo tồn rừng thông qua một vườn ươm cộng đồng.|Uncountable; nature conservation, conservation of forests. Conservation need not mean excluding all human use.|0
folklore|traditional-cultural-stories|NOUN|traditional stories and beliefs|Stories, beliefs and customs passed between generations within a community.|văn hóa dân gian; truyện kể và tín ngưỡng dân gian|The festival included a session on local folklore told by older residents.|Lễ hội có một buổi giới thiệu văn hóa dân gian địa phương do những cư dân lớn tuổi kể lại.|Uncountable; local folklore, a story from folklore. Broader than written folk literature alone.|-
import|goods-brought-in|NOUN|goods from another country|A product brought into a country from abroad.|hàng nhập khẩu|The shop placed local pottery beside imports from neighbouring countries.|Cửa hàng đặt đồ gốm trong nước cạnh hàng nhập khẩu từ các nước láng giềng.|Countable, often plural imports for goods. Distinguish an import from the activity of import.|0
import|bring-goods-from-abroad|VERB|bring goods from abroad|To bring goods into a country from another country.|nhập khẩu|The company imports fabric from several overseas suppliers.|Công ty nhập khẩu vải từ một số nhà cung cấp ở nước ngoài.|Transitive: import goods from a country, import into a market. Opposite direction to export.|1
import|activity-of-importing|NOUN|bringing goods into a country|The activity of bringing goods into a country from abroad.|việc nhập khẩu|The import of fresh produce requires careful transport planning.|Việc nhập khẩu nông sản tươi đòi hỏi lập kế hoạch vận chuyển cẩn thận.|Uncountable activity; the import of goods. In ordinary speech importing is also used.|2
